From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:11:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] test: repoint three guards whose pinned spelling was
 refactored (invariant intact)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Decision for all three: P - the guard pinned an output or a source line
that a later commit refactored; the invariant it protects was verified to
still hold by reading the new code path, so the guard now asserts that
invariant (behaviour where cheap) instead of the old spelling.

a-rename-is-neither-an-add-nor-a-remove "the column keeps its key and its
type" - culprit c219da21 (canonicalFieldKey: a column he names exactly
«المبلغ» / «التاريخ» gets the stable key amount / date, was money1 / date1).
Measured: before rename [text1:text, amount:number, date:date], after
[text1:text, amount:number, date:date] with the label now «القيمة». The test
now reads the keys from the build and asserts the rename keeps every key
AND type (the old pin never checked type).
  M8  rename assigns a new key  -> ✕  -   "amount:number",  +   "text4:number"
  M8b rename retypes the column -> ✕  -   "amount:number",  +   "amount:text"

schema-from-blueprint "Prompt 01 keeps the recognized expenses resource…"
- culprit c219da21, which taught the blueprint to read "a form to add an
expense with description, category, amount, and date" and moved the two
sibling Prompt 01 checks in api-project.test.ts to those four fields; this
third copy kept the stock five (title, amount, category, date, note).
apiColumnsForRequest is columnsFromFields(blueprintFor(...).fields), so the
test now asserts stored keys == rendered blueprint keys AND == his four.
  M9  server drops a rendered column (bp.fields.slice(1)) -> ✕  -   "description",
  M10 blueprint stops reading his form -> ✕ (received amount, category, date, note)

ai-schema "awaits the design" / "the interface builds its screens from the
SAME design" - culprits 3917fe1d (workflow apps skip the designer:
`designed = workflowApplication ? [] : await designDataModel(...)`) and
c219da21 (a non-promoted primary with its own columns also rides at the
head: `[...primaryModel, ...model]`); the third pin, masked behind the
first failure, was renamed by 76f66a5d (prevEntry -> apiEntry, the API
entry or the contract carried on a linked scaffold). The pins now name
the single exception and the wider head rule.
  M11 designer notes silenced -> ✕ Expected pattern: /const designed = workflowApplication…/
  M12 un-promoted primary dropped from the handoff -> ✕ Expected pattern: /const handedModel = …/
  M13 interface ignores the API model -> ✕ Expected pattern: /Array\.isArray\(apiEntry\?\.model\)…/
All restores: sha256 identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CSeapUrWatvdumdAwyPuqV
